<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayajidda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Abuyazidu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bayajidda is the legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa states</a> in the traditions of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. The story tells that he came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> by way of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a>, killed a snake that guarded a well at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daura">Daura</a>, and married its queen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daurama">Daurama</a>. Their son Bawo and his sons are said to have founded the seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa-bakwai">Hausa Bakwai</a> states, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a>, Katsina, Zazzau, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobir">Gobir</a> and Rano.</p></div>
